IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ks-types`
IMPORT `ks-membership`

-- KiwiSaver Act 2006 — GOAL 3: WITHDRAWALS (SCHEDULE 1, THE KIWISAVER
-- SCHEME RULES).
--
--   "Is the member permitted to withdraw for the purpose they give, and up
--    to how much?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2006_40.txt — Schedule 1,
-- clauses 4-14C.

§ `Goal 3 — withdrawals`

-- cl 8(1) "This clause applies to a member if the member has not made a
-- withdrawal under this clause before ... and,— (a) at least 3 years have
-- expired after the Commissioner received the first contribution ...; or (b)
-- the person has been a member of 1 or more KiwiSaver schemes or complying
-- superannuation funds for a combined total period of 3 years or more." (3)
-- "(b) ... (i) the land is, or is intended to be, the principal place of
-- residence ...; and (ii) the member has not, at any time before applying
-- ..., held an estate in land" (or (a) prescribed circumstances, or (c) a
-- qualifying person under the regulations).
@ref Schedule 1 cl 8(1), (3), (3B)
GIVEN w IS A `Withdrawal facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may make a first home withdrawal` w IF
        NOT w's `made a first home withdrawal before`
    AND w's `years since the first contribution or of membership` AT LEAST 3
    AND w's `the home is to be the principal residence`
    AND w's `has never held an estate in land, or qualifies otherwise`

-- cl 14(1) "no earlier than 1 year after the member's permanent emigration".
@ref Schedule 1 cl 14(1)
GIVEN w IS A `Withdrawal facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a year has passed since emigrating` w IF
    w's `applied on` AT LEAST `add years` (w's `emigrated on`) 1

@ref Schedule 1 cls 4-14C
@export The most a member may withdraw for a purpose under the KiwiSaver scheme rules (Schedule 1 of the KiwiSaver Act 2006, NZ): on reaching the superannuation qualification age, the accumulation (cl 4); at 60 and retired, the amount from an Australian scheme (cl 4B); for a first home, after 3 years and if never having held an estate in land, the accumulation less $1,000 and the Australian amount (cl 8); on death, the accumulation (cl 9); in significant financial hardship, the accumulation less Crown contributions, or the amount needed if the supervisor limits it (cl 10); in serious illness or a life-shortening congenital condition, the accumulation (cls 12, 12B); a year after permanent emigration (not to Australia), the accumulation less tax-credit Crown contributions and the Australian amount (cl 14); for tax on a foreign superannuation withdrawal, the liability up to the accumulation less Crown contributions (cl 14C). 0 where the rule is not met. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN w IS A `Withdrawal facts`  @desc The purpose, the member's age and whether they have reached the qualification age, the first-home facts, whether the manager or supervisor is satisfied of the ground and alternatives are exhausted, any limit to the amount needed, emigration and application dates, and any tax liability
      a IS A `Member account`  @desc The member's accumulation, the Crown contributions in it (all, and from tax credits), and the amount transferred from an Australian scheme
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the member may withdraw, facts` w `, account` a MEANS
    CONSIDER w's `purpose`
    WHEN `cl 4 reaching the New Zealand superannuation qualification age` THEN
        IF w's `qualification age reached` THEN accumulation ELSE 0
    WHEN `cl 4B amounts from an Australian scheme at 60 and retired` THEN
        IF w's `member aged` AT LEAST 60 AND w's `retired under the Australian rules` THEN a's `amount transferred from an Australian scheme` ELSE 0
    WHEN `cl 8 purchase of a first home` THEN
        IF `may make a first home withdrawal` w
        THEN max 0 (accumulation MINUS (1000 PLUS a's `amount transferred from an Australian scheme`))
        ELSE 0
    WHEN `cl 9 death` THEN accumulation
    WHEN `cl 10 significant financial hardship` THEN
        IF   w's `the manager or supervisor is satisfied of the ground` AND w's `alternative funding explored and exhausted`
        THEN CONSIDER w's `amount needed to alleviate the hardship`
             WHEN JUST needed THEN min needed lessCrown
             WHEN NOTHING THEN lessCrown
        ELSE 0
    WHEN `cl 12 serious illness` THEN
        IF w's `the manager or supervisor is satisfied of the ground` THEN accumulation ELSE 0
    WHEN `cl 12B a life-shortening congenital condition` THEN
        IF w's `the manager or supervisor is satisfied of the ground` THEN accumulation ELSE 0
    WHEN `cl 14 permanent emigration (other than to Australia)` THEN
        IF   `a year has passed since emigrating` w
        THEN max 0 (accumulation MINUS (a's `Crown contribution from tax credits in it` PLUS a's `amount transferred from an Australian scheme`))
        ELSE 0
    WHEN `cl 14C tax on a foreign superannuation withdrawal` THEN
        min (w's `tax or student loan liability`) lessCrown
    WHERE
        accumulation MEANS a's `member's accumulation`
        lessCrown    MEANS max 0 (accumulation MINUS a's `Crown contribution in it`)
